input.command:
cat > /tmp/r26.json <<'EOF'
{"commit_id":"fabb8d1a20c64a4cf4d91305519b254ca6c8d3c0","event":"COMMENT","comments":[
{"path":"scripts/rules.py","line":38,"side":"RIGHT","body":"This fails the maintainer lint: `ruff check` reports I001 (import block un-sorted) and `ruff format --check` wants to reformat the `try:` block. Separately, `_HAS_FCNTL` duplicates `fcntl is None`. If you set `fcntl = None` on ImportError, the call sites can check `if fcntl:`."},
{"path":"scripts/rules.py","start_line":949,"line":960,"side":"RIGHT","body":"On Windows this skips locking entirely. That brings back the race the lock exists to prevent: Claude Code runs PostToolUse hooks in parallel, so two `update_state` calls can each read the state, and the second save drops the first one's hunk. #23 proposes `msvcrt.locking(lock.fileno(), msvcrt.LK_LOCK, 1)` on the fallback path, and its author checked it with 8 concurrent writers. That fixes the crash and keeps the guarantee.\n\nYou also don't need to replace the `with` block. Closing the file releases the lock, so the explicit `LOCK_UN` and the `try/finally` add nothing. Keeping `with open(...) as lock:` and only branching the lock call gives a much smaller diff."}
]}
EOF
gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/26/reviews --input /tmp/r26.json --jq '.html_url'
cat > /tmp/r27.json <<'EOF'
{"commit_id":"2bb1e1c2dadb0b9b322e6aa4f7035d97b804b5f7","event":"COMMENT","comments":[
{"path":"scripts/rules.py","line":943,"side":"RIGHT","body":"No caller can act on \"callers on those platforms should serialize writes themselves\". The callers are this file's own hook entry points, which Claude Code starts concurrently, so serializing the writes is `update_state`'s job. Also, this docstring describes #26's behavior and is based on `main`, where the lock is never skipped. It belongs in #26. And if #26 switches to `msvcrt.locking` as #23 suggests, the original docstring is accurate on every platform and this change isn't needed."}
]}
EOF
gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/27/reviews --input /tmp/r27.json --jq '.html_url'

